  "source": "NEET 2024",
  "question": "In a vernier calipers, $(N + 1)$ divisions of vernier scale coincide with $N$ divisions of main scale. If $1$ MSD represents $0.1$ mm, the vernier constant (in cm) is :",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$100N$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$10(N + 1)$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{1}{10N}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{1}{100(N + 1)}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$(N + 1)\\ \\text{VSD} = N\\ \\text{MSD}$, so $1\\ \\text{VSD} = \\dfrac{N}{N + 1}\\ \\text{MSD}$.\n\n$$\\text{VC} = 1\\ \\text{MSD} - 1\\ \\text{VSD} = \\frac{1}{N + 1}\\ \\text{MSD} = \\frac{0.1\\ \\text{mm}}{N + 1} = \\frac{0.01\\ \\text{cm}}{N + 1} = \\frac{1}{100(N + 1)}\\ \\text{cm}$$",
